                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "05bda438-1c2f-33d8-b27a-0463bd86b281",
                        "entry_id": "0e85bdbd-cba9-33dc-8803-938e56ae4db5",
                        "glosses": [
                            "van rekeningen dat men de betaling kan opeisen; van rekeningen dat men ze kan innen"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c83b22e5-4844-445a-9e7f-4155e93d4709",
                                "sense_id": "05bda438-1c2f-33d8-b27a-0463bd86b281",
                                "text": "Door het gebruik van katvangers hopen de autobezitters te voorkomen dat hun identiteit bekend wordt bij overheidsinstanties. De katvanger krijgt de rekeningen, waardoor veel vorderingen door belasting en politie niet inbaar zijn. De eigenaar van de auto is vaak onbekend en moeilijk op te sporen. Zowel de katvanger als de auto-eigenaar zijn strafbaar."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "33356bba-5441-46c4-bcf4-3c0db8a874de",
                                "sense_id": "05bda438-1c2f-33d8-b27a-0463bd86b281",
                                "text": "Jaarlijks blijkt zo'n 70.000 euro niet inbaar, soms doordat de klant is overleden."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "82c9d4c8-0822-45da-8494-f276475ace65",
                                "sense_id": "05bda438-1c2f-33d8-b27a-0463bd86b281",
                                "text": "„Bestuurlijke boetes zijn wel leuk, maar ze zijn ook moeilijk inbaar”, aldus Suyver."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "bf52039d-642b-452d-8cf9-e17b623e1c0b",
                        "source_entry_id": "0e85bdbd-cba9-33dc-8803-938e56ae4db5",
                        "source_sense_id": "05bda438-1c2f-33d8-b27a-0463bd86b281",
                        "source_sense_description": "van rekeningen dat men de betaling kan opeisen; van rekeningen dat men ze kan innen",
                        "target_lang_word": "claimable",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "claimable",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d290a95b-93df-35eb-aaf0-9120dd7c1590",
                                        "entry_id": "1e211bfe-c525-3baa-8d6e-0611d0236662",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Able to be claimed."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "87bec94e-d5da-448e-b30e-2492ad22a735",
                                                "sense_id": "d290a95b-93df-35eb-aaf0-9120dd7c1590",
                                                "text": "1845 The New Statistical Account of Scotland\nThe existence of a legally claimable provision will, it is to be feared, tend everywhere more or less to produce its usual pernicious effects on the natural benevolence and moral independence of the people."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dd53ef01-5099-4b09-aa4e-d6aa7d12973c",
                                                "sense_id": "d290a95b-93df-35eb-aaf0-9120dd7c1590",
                                                "text": "If the insured party undertakes repair work himself or does it by independent sources this is not claimable from the insurance company."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "claimable",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "77fdd350-2d4b-3cfd-adf5-71784fde2bd1",
                                        "entry_id": "ea9529ac-a52e-3ea8-ae10-4b5dbf6f63d8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Something that can be claimed."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cae9e080-4300-4b7a-a686-2c8ec77f7104",
                                                "sense_id": "77fdd350-2d4b-3cfd-adf5-71784fde2bd1",
                                                "text": "The A.D.A. figures utilized in this study include the claimables for state aid plus the nonclaimables."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1d9c9e12-4a58-4640-becf-f63362885c41",
                                                "sense_id": "77fdd350-2d4b-3cfd-adf5-71784fde2bd1",
                                                "text": "So, for example, if the conditional and negation introduced in terms of pragmatic incompatibility really are a conditional and negation — letting us say that two claimables are inferentially related as premise and conclusion, or that they are incompatible — then what those locutions work on must be genuine propositional contents — what appears embedded as the antecedent of the conditional, or is negated."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7da03a51-65f8-4cd5-b56f-378a748e1172",
                                                "sense_id": "77fdd350-2d4b-3cfd-adf5-71784fde2bd1",
                                                "text": "But it does not follow that there were no true claimables."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "006c3d5f-a96c-4763-8b39-68da98269a31",
                        "source_entry_id": "0e85bdbd-cba9-33dc-8803-938e56ae4db5",
                        "source_sense_id": "05bda438-1c2f-33d8-b27a-0463bd86b281",
